with presidential elections just  five months off opponents of nicaragua's  president daniel ortega  and his wife rosalio murillo the vice  president  are dropping like flies  in recent weeks two opposition parties  were dissolved  and two candidates put under house  arrest under a new electoral reform  measure that the u.n high commissioner  for human rights  says will impede fair and free elections  now cristiana chamorro the most  competitive opposition candidate  is being accused of money laundering and  other crimes that would make her  ineligible to run she is the daughter of  former president joletta chamorro  who beat ortega in elections back in  1990  this is not about attacking me it's  about attacking the right of nicaraguans  to a fair  free and transparent election they want  to eliminate all of us  to frighten us all so we won't  participate  leaving the general prosecutor's office  chamorro said her lawyers were also  being threatened  nicaragua's pro-government prosecutor  says that the violeta chamorro  foundation that she leads  and which receives donations from abroad  to support  independent journalism is being  investigated for money laundering  over the weekend the vice president  confirmed that the foundation's  accountant  and its finance manager had been  arrested and will remain  imprisoned for up to 90 days while  they're investigated  the government has not responded to al  jazeera's request for comment  but vice president murillo says  opposition leaders are guilty of  organized crime  but that's not all at least a dozen  journalists  including the afp correspondent have  been detained  questioned or charged with possible  complicity  maria lilly delgado correspondent of the  us-based spanish language network u  division  says her bank accounts have also been  frozen  i asked the prosecutor what crime was i  being investigated for  and he said he would withhold that  information how am i supposed to defend  myself  the office of the independent news  organization confidential  has also been raided and shut down its  director carlos fernando chamorro  is cristiano chamorro's brother  we journalists practice journalism not  treason they destroyed everything  took all our equipment and arrested our  cameraman they're trying to crush  any voice that challenges the  dictatorship in our case journalists who  hold power to account  president ortega who controls all of  nicaragua's institutions  and who has the support of cuba and  venezuela is running for a fourth  consecutive term  and just like in venezuela the  opposition  will soon have to decide whether to  compete at all  in elections that they say have already  been decided  to see a newman al jazeera
 

